I'm playing a lot of monks right now, and I've begun to get in the
habit of removing the robe for the trip through the mines, due to risk
of losing it via poly trap.

I've noticed something that bothers me, though. Of course the tradeoff
is that by trying to save the robe for later (when I can learn and
cast more difficult spells), I have to live with a failure rate for
even simple healing/enchantment spells. Well, I thought, the best way
to deal with that is to practice until I get a skill level of "basic"
so I can cast "sleep" or "healing" risk-free.

But it doesn't work. I've just upgraded my monk to a basic level in
enchantment spells, and he has *exactly* the same failure rate he had
before -- 31%. The only armor being worn is leather gloves, leather
cloak, and low boots. Intelligence isn't high, but it's a reasonable
13. Protection is also 31%, with basic clerical spell skills.

What gives?

